A CHECK that rows already break: SQLite refuses the copy, nothing
changes. A CHECK is part of the CREATE's text alone: no pragma lists it,
which is why roux compares the text, never a reading of it.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 95), (2, 0);

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL CHECK (price_kr > 0)) STRICT;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `dish`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "dish" RENAME TO "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL CHECK (price_kr > 0)) STRICT
  table `dish`: its rows, by id, price_kr
    INSERT INTO "dish" ("id", "price_kr") SELECT "id", "price_kr" FROM "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_dish"

== error
migrating test.db: table `dish`: its rows, by id, price_kr: CHECK constraint failed: price_kr > 0
